From: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rda_combo: power the BT half on at init

rda_bt_power_on() and the per-chip sequences behind it have been ported since
the combo driver landed, but nothing ever called them: rda_combo_clients_ready()
brought up only the WLAN side. The chip's BT half therefore stayed unpowered,
so an HCI UART attached to it would have nothing to talk to.

Call it alongside the WLAN power-on. A failure is warned about but not fatal --
WLAN is why this driver exists, and a board with no BT antenna, or an
unpopulated combo variant, should still get wlan0.

This is the last device-side piece needed before the stock hci_uart driver can
be attached to the BT UART; see MODEM-WIFI-PORT.md section 29. Like the WLAN
power-on above it, it is a bring-up aid that belongs under rfkill eventually.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor driver, not upstream]
Signed-off-by: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/rdaw80211/rdacombodev/rda_combo_power_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/rdaw80211/rdacombodev/rda_combo_power_main.c
@@ -404,6 +404,22 @@ static void rda_combo_clients_ready(struct device *dev)
 		dev_warn(dev, "wifi power on failed\n");
 	else
 		dev_info(dev, "wifi powered on\n");
+
+	/*
+	 * Same for the BT half. Its power sequence has been ported since the
+	 * combo driver landed but nothing ever called it, so the chip's BT
+	 * side stayed dark and the HCI UART had nothing to talk to.
+	 *
+	 * Failure is not fatal: WLAN is the reason this driver exists, and a
+	 * board with no BT antenna or an unpopulated combo variant should
+	 * still get wlan0.
+	 *
+	 * TODO: move under rfkill, together with the WLAN side above.
+	 */
+	if (rda_bt_power_on())
+		dev_warn(dev, "bt power on failed\n");
+	else
+		dev_info(dev, "bt powered on\n");
 }
 
 static int rda_combo_client_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
